-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.12 (2026-10-25)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * NVIDIA's services (nvidia-persistenced, nvidia-powerd) run only while NVIDIA's driver is loaded, decided at every
    boot: a machine without an NVIDIA card skips them and is no longer "degraded"; a card added later starts them
    with no step, when udev loads the driver for it

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.10 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Programs that share CUDA with OpenGL, and NVIDIA's control panel, keep NVIDIA's own OpenGL when the session runs OpenGL on zink: their menu entries and their names in a terminal start through sparky-stereo-nvidia-opengl; the list starts with DaVinci Resolve and nvidia-settings, /etc/sparky-stereo/opengl-programs and ~/.config/sparky-stereo/opengl-programs add a program ("NAME nvidia") or give one back to zink ("NAME zink"), and the person's choice wins

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.9 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The system default for OpenGL stereo, from the graphics card the desktop runs on, written at install, at boot and when a card is added, removed or changes driver: when NVIDIA's driver runs the desktop, the session's programs run their OpenGL on Mesa over NVIDIA's Vulkan driver (zink) and get their two views with no launcher; KWin and Xwayland keep NVIDIA's driver; a desktop on Mesa keeps Mesa
  * sparky-stereo-opengl-default --opengl zink|nvidia sets the system choice; gl-stereo-run chooses per program

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.8 (2026-10-15)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Live sessions choose the NVIDIA driver at boot: the edition's open modules for Turing and newer, nouveau for older, mixed or unknown cards, for a kernel without the modules and for unsigned modules under Secure Boot; sparky.gpu=nvidia or sparky.gpu=nouveau overrides it
  * A notification says which driver runs the NVIDIA graphics in a live session, and why
  * KWin renders on a card that can render, with a screen connected, when the boot VGA device is a BMC's VGA chip
  * German, Japanese, Korean and Chinese (simplified and traditional) strings

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.7 (2026-10-12)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * French strings for the plan dialog, the menu entry and the policy message

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.6 (2026-10-11)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Install the NVIDIA userspace driver at the version of the edition's module (read from the module's version in the repository) instead of a fixed number

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.5 (2026-10-11)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Ship APT preferences that keep NVIDIA's container toolkit from looping between NVIDIA's two repositories
  * Prefer the edition's egl-wayland over the copy in NVIDIA's CUDA repository
  * Never install AMD's out-of-tree kernel driver or graphics userspace; ROCm updates normally

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.4 (2026-10-10)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Select hidraw access by exact sourced rig USB IDs
  * Install stable wheel drivers with headers matching the running kernel
  * Keep experimental drivers and Logitech replacements as visible candidates

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.3 (2026-10-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Enable PPD GPU clock and panel actions on matched AMD systems
  * Configure NVIDIA runtime power management only after a matched laptop driver install

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-10-05)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Print the CPU level, board, USB vendors and network PCI IDs as read-only facts
  * Name the firmware package a detected network card needs
  * Name Debian's broadcom-sta-dkms for a closed-driver Broadcom card without installing it

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-03)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Verify subsystem matches and headless localized GUI launch
  * Preserve fallback policy and report sensor and install failures

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-03)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Detect and configure matched hardware for Sparky Stereo OS
